यततामपि सिद्धानां कश्चिन्मां वेत्ति तत्त्वत: ॥ ३ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2106,\"bb\":1866,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1866/\",\"body_value\":\"manuṣyāṇāṁ sahasreṣu
kaścid yatati siddhaye
yatatām api siddhānāṁ
kaścin māṁ vetti tattvataḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2107,\"bb\":1867,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1867/\",\"shadow_value\":\"manuṣyāṇām – of men; sahasreṣu – out of many thousands; kaścit – someone; yatati – endeavors; siddhaye – for perfection; yatatām – of those so endeavoring; api – indeed; siddhānām – of those who have achieved perfection; kaścit – someone; mām – Me; vetti – does know; tattvataḥ – in fact.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"manuṣyāṇām\",\"translation\":\"of men\"},{\"word\":\"sahasreṣu\",\"translation\":\"out of many thousands\"},{\"word\":\"kaścit\",\"translation\":\"someone\"},{\"word\":\"yatati\",\"translation\":\"endeavors\"},{\"word\":\"siddhaye\",\"translation\":\"for perfection\"},{\"word\":\"yatatām\",\"translation\":\"of those so endeavoring\"},{\"word\":\"api\",\"translation\":\"indeed\"},{\"word\":\"siddhānām\",\"translation\":\"of those who have achieved perfection\"},{\"word\":\"kaścit\",\"translation\":\"someone\"},{\"word\":\"mām\",\"translation\":\"Me\"},{\"word\":\"vetti\",\"translation\":\"does know\"},{\"word\":\"tattvataḥ\",\"translation\":\"in fact\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2108,\"bb\":1868,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1868/\",\"body_value\":\"Out of many thousands among men, one may endeavor for perfection, and of those who have achieved perfection, hardly one knows Me in truth.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2109,\"bb\":1869,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1869/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2110,\"bb\":1870,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1870/\",\"body_value\":\"Kṛṣṇa is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the cause of all causes, the primeval Lord Govinda. Īśvaraḥ paramaḥ kṛṣṇaḥ sac-cid-ānanda-vigrahaḥ/ anādir ādir govindaḥ sarva-kāraṇa-kāraṇam. It is very difficult for the nondevotees to know Him. Although nondevotees declare that the path of bhakti, or devotional service, is very easy, they cannot practice it. If the path of bhakti is so easy, as the nondevotee class of men proclaim, then why do they take up the difficult path? Actually the path of bhakti is not easy. The so-called path of bhakti practiced by unauthorized persons without knowledge of bhakti may be easy, but when it is practiced factually according to the rules and regulations, the speculative scholars and philosophers fall away from the path. Śrīla Rūpa Gosvāmī writes in his Bhakti-rasāmṛta-sindhu (1.2.101):\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2111,\"bb\":1871,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1871/\",\"body_value\":\"śruti-smṛti-purāṇādi-
pañcarātra-vidhiṁ vinā
aikāntikī harer bhaktir
utpātāyaiva kalpate\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2112,\"bb\":1872,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1872/\",\"body_value\":\"“Devotional service of the Lord that ignores the authorized Vedic literatures like the Upaniṣads, Purāṇas and Nārada Pañcarātra is simply an unnecessary disturbance in society.”\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2113,\"bb\":1873,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1873/\",\"body_value\":\"$26\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2114,\"bb\":1874,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/3/b1874/\",\"body_value\":\"ataḥ śrī-kṛṣṇa-nāmādi
na bhaved grāhyam indriyaiḥ
