",\"title\":\"TEXT 5\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":2117,\"bb\":568153,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"भूमिरापोऽनलो वायु: खं मनो बुद्धिरेव च ।
अहङ्कार इतीयं मे भिन्ना प्रकृतिरष्टधा ॥ ४ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2118,\"bb\":1877,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/b1877/\",\"body_value\":\"bhūmir āpo ’nalo vāyuḥ
khaṁ mano buddhir eva ca
ahaṅkāra itīyaṁ me
bhinnā prakṛtir aṣṭadhā\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2119,\"bb\":1878,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/b1878/\",\"shadow_value\":\"bhūmiḥ – earth; āpaḥ – water; analaḥ – fire; vāyuḥ – air; kham – ether; manaḥ – mind; buddhiḥ – intelligence; eva – certainly; ca – and; ahaṅkāraḥ – false ego; iti – thus; iyam – all these; me – My; bhinnā – separated; prakṛtiḥ – energies; aṣṭadhā – eightfold.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"bhūmiḥ\",\"translation\":\"earth\"},{\"word\":\"āpaḥ\",\"translation\":\"water\"},{\"word\":\"analaḥ\",\"translation\":\"fire\"},{\"word\":\"vāyuḥ\",\"translation\":\"air\"},{\"word\":\"kham\",\"translation\":\"ether\"},{\"word\":\"manaḥ\",\"translation\":\"mind\"},{\"word\":\"buddhiḥ\",\"translation\":\"intelligence\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"ahaṅkāraḥ\",\"translation\":\"false ego\"},{\"word\":\"iti\",\"translation\":\"thus\"},{\"word\":\"iyam\",\"translation\":\"all these\"},{\"word\":\"me\",\"translation\":\"My\"},{\"word\":\"bhinnā\",\"translation\":\"separated\"},{\"word\":\"prakṛtiḥ\",\"translation\":\"energies\"},{\"word\":\"aṣṭadhā\",\"translation\":\"eightfold\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2120,\"bb\":1879,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/b1879/\",\"body_value\":\"Earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intelligence and false ego – all together these eight constitute My separated material energies.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2121,\"bb\":1880,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/b1880/\",\"body_value\":\"The science of God analyzes the constitutional position of God and His diverse energies. Material nature is called prakṛti, or the energy of the Lord in His different puruṣa incarnations (expansions) as described in the Nārada Pañcarātra, one of the Sātvata-tantras:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2122,\"bb\":1881,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/b1881/\",\"body_value\":\"viṣṇos tu trīṇi rūpāṇi
puruṣākhyāny atho viduḥ
ekaṁ tu mahataḥ sraṣṭṛ
dvitīyaṁ tv aṇḍa-saṁsthitam
tṛtīyaṁ sarva-bhūta-sthaṁ
tāni jñātvā vimucyate\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2123,\"bb\":1882,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/b1882/\",\"body_value\":\"“For material creation, Lord Kṛṣṇa’s plenary expansion assumes three Viṣṇus. The first one, Mahā-viṣṇu, creates the total material energy, known as the mahat-tattva. The second, Garbhodaka-śāyī Viṣṇu, enters into all the universes to create diversities in each of them. The third, Kṣīrodaka-śāyī Viṣṇu, is diffused as the all-pervading Supersoul in all the universes and is known as Paramātmā. He is present even within the atoms. Anyone who knows these three Viṣṇus can be liberated from material entanglement.”\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2124,\"bb\":1883,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/b1883/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2125,\"bb\":1884,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/4/b1884/\",\"body_value\":\"$26\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 7.4\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 7.4\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2b:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n31:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n27:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"